# Terraform
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
# Committed on purpose, and checked. It holds no secrets -- only the structural
# flags whose defaults mean "off", which is why leaving it out of git turned an
# ordinary `terraform apply` into something that would destroy the Cognito pool
# and the DKIM records and call it a plan. The blanket *.tfvars rule is the
# right default and this is the deliberate exception; see the file's own header
# for what is in it and what is not.
!terraform/app/terraform.tfvars
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Node / frontend
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.claude/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
